  "responseText": "{\"reviewedAffectedSlots\":[\"W031\",\"W103\",\"W127\"],\"findings\":[\"W031 (nnxyz nifty faces #17): Correctly composited over white canvas reveals a teal/cyan ground — not a dark or neutral field. The stacked rectangular zones carry lime green as the dominant line color, with magenta, red, orange-yellow, and white strokes throughout. The hat zone at top is a densely cross-hatched rectangle against that open teal. The eye zone holds circular spiral forms rather than purely rectangular frames. The mouth zone is a white-ground rectangle with dense parallel lines. The overall palette is bright and open, not pressurized against a dark surround. Previous description referenced 'lime, magenta, and red' correctly but omitted the prominent teal ground and the white interior of the mouth zone, and overstated the rectangular rigidity of the eye compartment which contains spiral-circular marks.\",\"W103 (nnxyz nifty faces #4): Correctly composited over white canvas reveals a light, open ground — cyan-blue, lavender, and yellow color patches fill the head zone with no dark surround. Round glasses rendered in blue and white sit centrally on a face built from cyan, orange, red, and yellow patches. Radiating lines extend outward in cyan, magenta, yellow-green, and white against a pale background, not against darkness. The face is luminous and open rather than holding center against a dark field. The previous description's phrase 'the previous face was absorbed into darkness' (transition from W111) is accurate for W111, but the description of W103 itself implied a dark or compressed surround that the corrected image does not show — the radiating lines escape into a light, multi-colored field.\",\"W127 (nnxyz nifty faces #6): Correctly composited over white canvas reveals that the background between and beyond the line structures is white and light gray, not a dark or opaque fill. The dominant structural lines are thick yellow, red, cyan/blue, and white, forming nested rectangles and a large downward triangle in the lower half. The left eye zone contains a blue X-like form and small rectangular marks; the right eye zone is a yellow-and-cyan rounded rectangle with red diagonal strokes inside. Green zigzag marks sit inside the lower triangle. Purple cross-hatching appears at the margins but the overall field is bright and open. The previous description mentioned 'loose scattered strokes overflow the face boundary' — confirmed — but 'hard-edged rectangles lock the eye zones' needs refinement: the left zone is more angular/X-framed while the right is a rounded rectangle. The ground between strokes reads as white, not as a compressed or dark field.\"],\"membershipConcerns\":[],\"corrections\":[{\"slot\":\"W031\",\"whyHere\":\"Stacked rectangular zones — a cross-hatched hat block, a brow-and-eye band containing spiral-circular marks, and a white-ground mouth rectangle — each packed with lime green, magenta, red, orange, and white lines against an open teal ground; the face becomes a column of distinct compartments, each with its own internal density.\",\"transitionFromPrevious\":\"The previous bands interrupted a recognizable head rendered against a light field; here the face is rebuilt entirely from stacked rectangular zones on a flat teal ground, so the compartmentalization is now the structure, not an overlay.\"},{\"slot\":\"W103\",\"whyHere\":\"Round glasses anchor a frontal face assembled from cyan, orange, red, and yellow color patches; scribbled lines in cyan, magenta, yellow-green, and white radiate outward beyond the head's outline in all directions into a pale, open field — the face holds center while the mark system expands freely around it.\",\"transitionFromPrevious\":\"The previous face was absorbed into a dark mass; here a frontal presence reasserts itself in a luminous, open field, but the radiating lines suggest the face is actively losing its boundary to the marks surrounding it.\"},{\"slot\":\"W127\",\"whyHere\":\"Thick yellow, red, and cyan lines form nested rectangles and a large downward triangle across the lower half, with a blue angular frame around the left eye zone and a rounded yellow-cyan rectangle enclosing the right; green zigzag marks fill the triangle's interior while white and purple cross-hatched strokes overflow the face boundary into the open white ground beyond.\",\"transitionFromPrevious\":\"The previous face was compressed inward against a flat purple field; here the rigid frames are surrounded by lines that refuse to stay inside the figure's edges, the face pushing back outward into an open, light ground.\"}],\"chapterCorrections\":[]}",
